From: Eternal Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] testsuite: aarch64: use GCC13 extension order in native_cpu_36

The PR124629 test was backported from upstream commit
b41352c7aa2645de6c5751d447589c2ef8c4fa4d (GCC13 backport
38ac911b5f1c7d81f375cb4253336ed1c713967f). GCC13.5 emits crc before
dotprod for this feature set. Keep the exact architecture, all four
extensions, and end-of-line assertion; correct only their expected order.

Observed with published Eternal GCC13.5 and reproduced by the GCC13 ARM
source-suite failure in CI run44014032027. No production compiler change.
Upstream provenance:
https://gcc.gnu.org/pipermail/gcc-cvs/2026-August/459694.html

--- a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_36.c
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_36.c
@@ -7,4 +7,4 @@
   return 0;
 }
 
-/* { dg-final { scan-assembler {\.arch armv8-a\+dotprod\+crc\+crypto\+sve2\n} } } */
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler {\.arch armv8-a\+crc\+dotprod\+crypto\+sve2\n} } } */
